The task is `fizz_buzz(n)`: count every decimal digit `7` among nonnegative integers below `n` that are divisible by 11 or 13. I’m using only integer assignments, `while`, `if`, `%`, `//`, comparisons, and Boolean `or`, which keeps both the implementation and the semantics compact enough for a symbolic proof.
