codex
All three examples execute to the required results (`0`, `2`, and `3`). For the symbolic phase I’m expressing two reusable loop invariants: the inner loop counts the sevens in one integer, and the outer loop accumulates that contribution across the interval. This lets `kprove` reason inductively instead of unrolling an unbounded input.
